The modern form is almost solely intended to transcribe the ancient character shown in the image. Various transcriptions can be found, sometimes with {{zh-l|*八}} replacing the component {{lang|zh|亼}} (cf. {{zh-m|*今}}, which contained this component historically). The bottom component, originally {{zh-m|*艸|gloss=grass}} duplicating the top component, may be modernised as {{zh-l|*廾}}, though some may omit it.

===Pronunciation===
Unclear. It is probable that {{och-l|方}} was the intended phonetic component. The character has been romanized as "Pang" in the literature, and a comparison with a place attested as {{lang|zh|方}} in the ''{{w|Classic of Poetry}}'' has been made.<ref>{{cite-book|author=Li, Feng|authorlink=Li Feng (sinologist)|title=Landscape and Power in Early China: The Crisis and Fall of the Western Zhou|year=2006|pages=56|publisher=Cambridge University Press|location=Cambridge, UK|isbn=978-0-511-34848-8}}</ref>

